	abstract = {Iron ore logistics generates fugitive PM<sub>2</sub>.<sub>5</sub> emissions that penetrate adjacent urban environments, yet their infiltration into naturally ventilated tropical residences remains poorly characterized. We investigate indoor-outdoor PM<sub>2</sub>.<sub>5</sub> dynamics near the Tubarão Port Complex (Vitória, Brazil) through a 170-day paired campaign (May–October 2019, n = 114 valid pairs). Two vertically separated sites (P1 outdoor at 2 m; P2 indoor at 17 m, 160 m apart) define the Elevated Accumulation Ratio (EAR = C<sub>indoor</sub>/C<sub>outdoor</sub>) as a relative accumulation index; because Black Carbon shows the opposite vertical behavior (EAR_BC = 0.70), the observed EAR >1 is interpreted as a conservative lower bound on indoor accumulation rather than a height artefact. Mean PM<sub>2.5</sub> was 7.33 μg m<sup>−3</sup> indoors and 5.78 μg m<sup>−3</sup> outdoors (Wilcoxon p < 0.001; median EAR = 1.25; ≈66 % of pairs exceeding unity). APCA identified vehicular emissions as dominating outdoor mass (63.6 %; confirmatory solution, KMO = 0.77); the exploratory indoor solution (KMO = 0.62, n = 38) indicated indoor air governed by port-associated sources, secondary sulfate (38.3 %), and soil resuspension (27.5 %). Geochemical profiling identified Fe/Si decoupling, confirming an industrial origin distinct from local ferrolaterite soils. Screening-level USEPA health risk assessment yielded a Cr-driven excess lifetime cancer risk of 4.5 × 10<sup>−6</sup> under a realistic 15 % Cr (VI) assumption (cumulative ELCR including Co and Ni: approximately 9.2 × 10<sup>−6</sup>), rising to 3.0 × 10<sup>−5</sup> under a conservative 100 % Cr (VI) worst-case scenario (cumulative: 3.5 × 10<sup>−5</sup>, below the 10<sup>−4</sup> ceiling under all scenarios evaluated). At this receptor, static buffer zones showed limited effectiveness under the coastal wind fields observed, indicating that mitigation should be adaptively modulated by real-time meteorology; confirmation across multiple dwellings is required before generalizing to port-adjacent tropical residences. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.},
