	abstract = {Urban aesthetics is one of the main components that can contribute in improving the urban gloomy picture by strengthening the formation of public space, in this case, green open space which in accordance to the demands of the community. The study of cities and its relationship to green open space particularly its effects on the well-being, health, happiness, and satisfaction of city residents with their environment is a topic that has received a lot of attention. This study seeks to examine the factors of landscape elements that do not contribute to or reduce the aesthetic value of the appearance of green open space, by exploring the perception of visitors. This study also seeks to show the role of landscape elements in improving aesthetic configurations and social functions to meet the needs of society. This research was conducted using a survey method with descriptive analysis. Data collection was carried out by observation and documentation techniques. The study’s results indicate that landscape elements, including jogging tracks, fences, field grass, and seating, are critical components in aesthetic assessments that gave the least contribution to aesthetic image of green open space. © The Author(s) 2025.},
