	abstract = {This paper examines the relevance of the media coverage in relation to changes in urban development in Germany predicted at the onset of the Covid-19 pandemic. Mass media, due to the speed and mass of its dissemination, has a great impact on a wide audience and its perception. From a social constructivist perspective and the analytical view of the three worlds theory, we use a media content analysis to examine how media communication constructs pandemic-related impacts on urban development – the Post-Covid-City. It is reported that there is a particular need for action in downtowns and brick-and-mortar retail, an increase in the importance of public green and open spaces, and increased attention to the concept of resilient urban development – thus focusing mainly on material world 1 changes. In general, it is conveyed that the Covid-19 pandemic has led to a change in perspective and a questioning of existing concepts of urban development. © 2024 FRANZ STEINER VERLAG GMBH. All rights reserved.},
