	abstract = {There is a significant regional difference of agricultural insurance development across China. This paper uses China's provincial panel data in East, Central and West regions to examine six group variables: risk perception, risk management, agricultural insurance recognition, agricultural insurance trust, agricultural insurance affordability and agricultural production affection, and their effects on agricultural insurance development in different regions. The results show that there is no such thing as a "Samaritan Dilemma" in farmers' agricultural insurance decision-making; agricultural insurance affordability is one of the fundamental factors that influence its development; risk perception significantly influences agricultural insurance development in east provinces, whereas the affection variable is one of the most influencing factors in central provinces. In the west region, risk management is most important. To promote balanced development of agricultural insurance across China, the government may need to implement a variety of policies, sensitive to regional preferences. © 2016, DAV College. All rights reserved.},
