	affiliations = {Discipline of Geographical and Environmental Studies, The University of Adelaide, Adelaide, SA, Australia},
	abstract = {This study investigates the risk perceptions of environmental experts and the general public to selected environmental threats in Adelaide, South Australia. Adelaide is one of the most seismically active cities in Australia and has experienced earthquakes and landslides. The Mediterranean climate makes Adelaide more prone to climate change, which may exacerbate flash flooding, heatwaves, severe storms and droughts. It is also the driest capital city in Australia and the area around the city is a very hazardous bushfire region. Metropolitan Adelaide is unique from many other urban environments in Australia due to its elevated exposure to a variety of environmental risks. A random sample of members of the public and of environmental experts in metropolitan Adelaide completed a questionnaire regarding their perceptions towards these specific environmental risks and the factors that influence their perceptions. In contrast to overseas studies, which found marked discrepancies between expert and public perceptions of risk, this study found a very strong positive correlation between expert and public perceptions of environmental risk in metropolitan Adelaide.},
